    <templateId root="2.16.840.1.113883.10.20.22.2.9" extension="2014-06-09"/>
    <code code="51847-2" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="Evaluation + Plan note"/>
    <title>Assessment and Plan</title>
    <text><list listType="ordered"><item><content styleCode="Bold">Obsessive-compulsive disorder, early improvement (F42.2)</content>. Y-BOCS 24, down 14 percent from 28: early improvement, well short of a response, which in OCD often takes eight to twelve weeks or more. PHQ-9 6 and GAD-7 10. Suicide risk remains low. [S]<list><item>Increase sertraline to 100 mg each morning; nurse telephone check in two weeks for side effects.</item><item>Continue weekly ERP, adding counting and repeating targets.</item><item>Collaborative safety plan reviewed and unchanged; 988 Suicide &amp; Crisis Lifeline and the clinic number confirmed.</item></list></item><item><content styleCode="Bold">Underweight from food rituals (R63.6)</content>. Up 0.8 kg since intake to 64.6 kg. [S]<list><item>Three meals a day; one meal a day without calculating as an exposure task.</item></list></item><item><content styleCode="Bold">Insufficient sleep (Z72.820)</content>. About five hours a night. [S]<list><item>Keep the sleep diary; no laboratory work after midnight.</item></list></item></list><paragraph>Protocol monitoring: items the monitoring protocol calls for at this visit. [S]</paragraph><table><thead><tr><th>Domain</th><th>Measure</th><th>Interval</th><th>Status</th><th>Detail</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Survey</td><td>Y-BOCS severity score (recorded in the note; no LOINC code found)</td><td>At baseline and about every 4 to 6 weeks during acute treatment</td><td>Completed today</td><td>24, down 14 percent from 28; dose increased</td></tr><tr><td>Survey</td><td>PHQ-9 and GAD-7 for secondary depression and anxiety</td><td>At baseline and periodically while depressive or anxiety symptoms are present</td><td>Completed today</td><td>PHQ-9 6 (item 9 scored 0); GAD-7 10</td></tr><tr><td>Survey</td><td>Suicide risk reassessment (C-SSRS Since Last Visit and PHQ-9 item 9 when given)</td><td>Every visit during acute treatment</td><td>Completed today</td><td>No suicidal thoughts, intent, plan, or behavior since the last visit; PHQ-9 item 9 scored 0. Safety plan reviewed</td></tr><tr><td>Medication safety</td><td>Sertraline adherence and adverse effects (nausea, diarrhea, sleep, activation, sexual effects)</td><td>Every visit and two weeks after each dose increase</td><td>Completed today</td><td>No side effects since week one; no missed doses; dose increased to 100 mg, with a nurse call in two weeks</td></tr><tr><td>Self-management</td><td>Exposure and response prevention attendance and homework</td><td>Every visit during acute treatment</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Five sessions; door handles without washing for ten minutes; two meals a week without calculating</td></tr><tr><td>Examination</td><td>Weight and BMI</td><td>Every visit while underweight</td><td>Completed today</td><td>64.6 kg, BMI 18.3, up 0.8 kg</td></tr><tr><td>Examination</td><td>Hand skin</td><td>Every visit while dermatitis is present</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Dry; no fissures</td></tr><tr><td>Self-management</td><td>Sleep diary</td><td>Every visit during acute treatment</td><td>Completed today</td><td>About five hours a night</td></tr><tr><td>Medication safety</td><td>Antipsychotic augmentation monitoring (weight, glucose, lipids, movement)</td><td>Only if an antipsychotic is added</td><td>Not indicated</td><td>No augmentation; responding to sertraline and ERP</td></tr></tbody></table><paragraph>Goal progress:</paragraph><list><item>Y-BOCS down by at least 35 percent (treatment response) by twenty-four weeks. In progress; target 1902-06-30 [S]</item><item>Rituals under one hour a day, with meals eaten without calculating. In progress; target 1902-06-30 [S]</item><item>BMI at least 18.5 with three meals a day. In progress; target 1902-06-30 [S]</item><item>Hands healed, with washing under 15 times a day. In progress; target 1902-04-07 [S]</item><item>At least six hours of sleep most nights. In progress; target 1902-06-30 [S]</item></list><paragraph>Guideline basis: Practice Guideline for the Treatment of Patients With Obsessive-Compulsive Disorder (2007); Guideline Watch: Practice Guideline for the Treatment of Patients With Obsessive-Compulsive Disorder (2013); Obsessive-compulsive disorder and body dysmorphic disorder: treatment (CG31) (2005); VA/DoD Clinical Practice Guideline for Assessment and Management of Patients at Risk for Suicide (2024)</paragraph><paragraph>Follow-up: Review in six weeks. Next scheduled visit 1902-04-07: twelve-week OCD treatment review. [S]</paragraph></text>

  </section>
